.\" Manpage for bob (Bodyguard Of Bits)
.\" Format: man-7 (groff_man). Render with: man -l man/bob.1
.\" Contact: cedricclauzel30@gmail.com to correct errors or typos.
.TH BOB 1 "2026-05-17" "BOB 0.4.6" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
bob \- Bodyguard Of Bits, a Linux hardening auditor with CIS benchmark mapping
.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sudo bob
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B bob
audits a Linux system against a curated set of hardening checks (firewall,
SSH, kernel sysctl, services, file permissions, MAC policy, auditd, …) and
reports findings with severity levels (OK / INFO / WARN / ALERT). It produces
a colourised terminal summary, an optional detailed log file, and an optional
JSON output for scripting.
.PP
.B bob
is audit-only: it never modifies system state without explicit user
confirmation (see
.B \-\-fix
and
.B \-\-apply
below). The
.B \-\-offline
mode disables all outbound network calls and is recommended for distro
build sandboxes and air-gapped environments.
.PP
Most checks require root for full coverage (reading
.IR /etc/shadow ,
parsing UFW rules, querying
.B systemctl
state). Use
.B sudo bob
in normal operation.
.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS Audit control
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Show detailed port exposure per service in the services section.
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-detailed
Write a detailed audit report to the configured log directory
.RI ( ~/.local/share/bob/logs/
by default).
.TP
.B \-\-target=\fIN\fR
Set a security score target in 1\(en10. When the resulting score is below
.IR N ,
.B bob
exits with code
.B 4
(see
.B EXIT CODES
below). Useful in CI.
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Suppress all terminal output. Use the exit code to detect issues.
Implies neither
.B \-d
nor
.BR \-\-json .
.TP
.BR \-\-no\-color
Disable ANSI escape sequences in terminal output.
.
.SS Output formats
.TP
.BR \-j ", " \-\-json
Emit the audit summary to standard output as JSON
.RB ( schema_version
.BR \(dq1\(dq ).
Suppresses the human-readable terminal box. See
.B JSON OUTPUT
below.
.TP
.BR \-J ", " \-\-json\-full
Like
.BR \-\-json ,
but includes per-finding, per-service, per-port detail (large payload).
.TP
.B \-\-format=\fIFMT\fR
Where
.I FMT
is
.BR text " (default), "
.BR json ", or "
.BR markdown .
.
.SS Configuration and i18n
.TP
.B \-\-lang=\fICODE\fR
Set interface language. Currently supported:
.B en
(default) and
.BR fr .
When neither
.B \-\-lang
nor
.B \-\-french
is given,
.B bob
auto-detects the locale from
.BR LC_ALL ,
.BR LC_MESSAGES ,
or
.B LANG
(POSIX precedence). Falls back to English on
.BR C ,
.BR POSIX ,
or an unsupported locale.
.TP
.B \-\-french
Shorthand for
.BR \-\-lang=fr .
Overrides the locale detection.
.TP
.B \-\-reconfigure
Re-run the first-launch configuration wizard (custom service ports, log dir).
.TP
.B \-\-profile=\fINAME\fR
Apply an audit profile that adjusts severity overrides per finding key.
Built-in profiles:
.BR server " (default), "
.BR desktop ", "
.BR container .
User profiles in
.IR ~/.config/bob/profiles/*.conf
take precedence. See
.BR bob-profile (5).
.
.SS Comparison and history
.TP
.B \-\-diff
Show only the delta vs the previous audit (new findings, resolved findings,
score change). The baseline lives at
.IR ~/.config/bob/last_baseline.json .
.TP
.B \-\-history
Display a sparkline of the last 50 audit scores from
.IR ~/.config/bob/history.jsonl .
.TP
.B \-\-breakdown ", " \-B
After the audit, print the complete score computation (deductions, caps,
per-domain scores). Useful for understanding why the final score is what
it is.
.
.SS Remediation
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-fix
Enter interactive fix mode: each finding with a remediation command prompts
the user with
.RB \(dq y/N \(dq.
.B bob
NEVER runs a command without explicit user confirmation.
.TP
.B \-\-apply
Like
.BR \-\-fix ,
but assume
.B y
for every prompt. Use with extreme caution; intended for unattended fix runs
where the user has reviewed
.BR \-\-explain
beforehand.
.TP
.B \-\-explain=\fIKEY\fR
Display a structured explanation for a single finding key. Pass
.B list
as the
.I KEY
to list all available explain keys (112 keys in v0.4.x).
.TP
.B \-e
Shortcut for
.BR \-\-explain= .
.
.SS Network and integrations
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-offline
Disable all outbound network calls (public IP lookup, webhook POST). Required
for distro build sandboxes; recommended for air-gapped environments.
.TP
.BR \-w ", " \-\-webhook=\fIURL\fR
POST the audit summary as JSON to
.IR URL
after the audit. Skipped if
.B \-\-offline
is given.
.TP
.B \-\-webhook-format=\fIFMT\fR
.I FMT
is
.BR auto " (default — Slack/generic detection from the URL), "
.BR generic ", or "
.BR slack .
.
.SS Periodic audits
.TP
.B \-\-install\-cron
Run an interactive wizard to install a cron job that audits the system on
a schedule and emails the report.
.TP
.B \-\-manage\-cron
Manage installed cron jobs (list, edit schedule/email, delete).
.TP
.B \-\-watch=\fIN\fR
Re-run the audit every
.I N
seconds until interrupted with Ctrl\-C. Live-monitoring mode.
.
.SS Filters
.TP
.B \-\-check=\fIA,B,…\fR
Run only the named sections (prefix matching:
.B kernel
matches
.BR kernel_hardening " and " kernel_modules ).
Core checks
.RB ( firewall ,
.BR ports ,
.BR services ,
.BR logs )
always run.
.TP
.B \-\-skip=\fIA,B,…\fR
Inverse of
.BR \-\-check .
.TP
.B \-\-list\-checks
Print all available section names.
.
.SS Misc
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print BOB version and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print help.
.TP
.B \-\-install\-completion
Install bash completion to
.IR /etc/bash_completion.d/bob .
.TP
.B \-\-manage\-logs
Manage stored audit reports (list, view, delete) in
.IR ~/.local/share/bob/logs/ .
.TP
.B \-\-ignore=\fIKEY\fR
Persistently ignore finding
.I KEY
across all future audits. Stored in
.IR ~/.config/bob/ignore.yml .
.
.SH EXIT CODES
Stable public API. These codes do not change within a major version; new
codes may be added but never removed.
.TP
.B 0
Clean audit \(em no alerts, no warnings.
.TP
.B 1
Warnings detected (improvements suggested).
.TP
.B 2
Alerts detected \(em action required.
.TP
.B 3
Technical error (CLI parsing, IO, internal).
.TP
.B 4
.B \-\-target=\fIN\fR
specified and score < N.
.
.SH JSON OUTPUT
.B \-\-json
emits a stable JSON contract (see
.B schema_version
.BR \(dq1\(dq ).
Top-level keys:
.IR schema_version ,
.IR version ,
.IR host ,
.IR timestamp ,
.IR score ,
.IR score_max ,
.IR risk ,
.IR network_context ,
.IR public_ip ,
.IR alerts ,
.IR warnings ,
.IR deductions ,
.IR domain_scores .
Full mode
.RB ( \-\-json\-full )
adds
.IR findings ,
.IR services ,
.IR open_ports ,
.IR firewall_stack ,
.IR hardening ,
.IR ipv6 .
.PP
Each deduction and finding carries a stable dotted
.B key
(e.g.
.BR firewall.logging_off )
and an optional
.B template_vars
dict for locale-independent reconstruction of the message via
.B bob.formatter.format_finding .
.PP
See
.IR DOCUMENTS/README_TECH.md " section " "JSON output schema"
for the complete reference.
.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/bob/config.conf
User configuration (custom ports, log directory, SUID whitelist). Mode 0600.
See
.BR bob.conf (5).
.TP
.I ~/.config/bob/profiles/*.conf
User audit profiles (severity overrides per finding key). See
.BR bob-profile (5).
.TP
.I ~/.config/bob/services.d/*.json
User service plugin definitions. JSON Schema:
.IR bob/data/schemas/service.schema.json .
.TP
.I ~/.config/bob/checks.d/*.py
Custom Python audit plugins. NOT sandboxed.
.TP
.I ~/.config/bob/last_baseline.json
Snapshot of the previous audit for
.B \-\-diff
comparisons.
.TP
.I ~/.config/bob/history.jsonl
Append-only score history (rotated at 1000 entries).
.TP
.I ~/.config/bob/ignore.yml
Persistently ignored finding keys.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/bob/logs/
Default detailed-report destination
.RB ( \-d
flag).
.TP
.I /etc/cron.d/bob-NAME
System cron entries installed via
.BR \-\-install\-cron .
.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B SUDO_USER
Honored by BOB to resolve
.RB \(dq ~/.config/bob/ \(dq
to the invoking user's home rather than
.IR /root/
when run via
.BR sudo .
.TP
.BR LC_ALL ", " LC_MESSAGES ", " LANG
Used for locale auto-detection (POSIX precedence). See
.BR \-\-lang
above.
.TP
.B BOB_SHARE
Absolute path to BOB's installed share directory (containing
.IR locales/ ", " data/ ", etc.).
Set by the installer entry point — typical values:
.IR /usr/share/bob/
(distro packages) or
.IR /usr/local/share/bob/
(local installs). When unset, BOB uses the data files bundled inside the
Python package itself (pipx / pip install layout).
.TP
.B UFW_AUDIT_SHARE
Legacy alias for
.BR BOB_SHARE ,
retained for backward compatibility with pre-v0.4.2 installer scripts. Will
be removed in a future major release.
.BR BOB_SHARE
takes precedence when both are set.
.
.SH SECURITY
BOB is an audit-only tool that runs with root privileges. It is part of the
.B post-compromise
audit toolchain: a rooted attacker can already lie to BOB about every value
it reads from
.IR /proc/ ", " /sys/ ", " /etc/ .
BOB does not replace a file-integrity scanner (AIDE, Tripwire), an antivirus
(ClamAV), nor a rootkit detector (rkhunter).
.PP
See the project's
.B SECURITY.md
file for the complete threat model and the vulnerability disclosure process.
.
